 ```
 
-`--sort` and `--direction` select the ordering column and direction; both default
-to a timestamp descending sort. Results are unpaginated.
+`--action` is optional; omit it to match every action for `--actor`.
 
-Clause building lives in `auditlog.filters`, so the same escaping and ordering
-rules apply to every query against the table.
+`--sort` and `--direction` select the ordering column and direction. `--sort` accepts
+any audit table column (`id`, `actor`, `action`, `target`, `ts`) and `--direction` accepts
+`asc` or `desc`; both default to a timestamp descending sort.
+
+`--since` filters to rows whose timestamp is at or after the given ISO date
+(e.g. `--since 2026-01-01`).
+
+`--limit` and `--offset` paginate the (sorted) results. `--limit` defaults to 50 rows
+and `--offset` defaults to 0.
+
+```sh
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m auditlog.search --actor alice --since 2026-01-01 \
+  --sort actor --direction asc --limit 20 --offset 40
+```
+
+Clause building lives in `auditlog.filters`, so the same validation and ordering
+rules apply to every query against the table. `--sort`/`--direction` are checked
+against an allowlist of table columns and `asc`/`desc` before being used to build
+the query, since column names can't be passed as bound parameters; all other values
+(`--actor`, `--action`, `--since`, `--limit`, `--offset`) are passed as bound
+parameters.
